{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_xP6uWdz57u8q9M2SOgxg6DbO","content":"1\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-02 2x:xx +0700\n2\tCoding-Agent: kimi\n3\tSession: fresh (read-only architect re-audit)\n4\tMode: read-only\n5\t\n6\t# Task: the checkpoint-B re-audit — yang.php P4 S8 (the generator runtime) and the S7 fixture package\n7\t\n8\tRole: architect. You ruled the original checkpoint-B conditions (ruling 7 and the heap ruling chain). Re-audit the branch against them; if satisfied, checkpoint B CLOSES and the P4 landing proceeds.\n9\t\n10\tBranch: yang-php-p4 @ 82b78294, worktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-php-p4 (read-only for you).\n11\t\n12\t## The evidence chain since your rulings\n13\t\n14\t1. The fold reconciliation (304ef51e): the recorded/pending/generator assertions state the true post-fold invariants; awaiting-oracle equals exactly the enabled :pending set; recorded :out/:diag/:uncaught cross-checked per fixture.\n15\t2. The heap chain: your r2 diagnosis (php/gen-enter chained :resume/:ctx continuations across resumes) -> the fix 4c8eaacf (running/suspended states rebuilt with live fields only; yield snapshots and gen-put! returns dropped) -> the corrected fixture (18ef324d: normal completion, the cycle-rooted generator as the sole extra root) -> the gate: 99 cells at N=10 AND N=1000 on all four VMs, identical deep sizes per VM.\n16\t3. The stress re-tiering (e42b2844 + 1347824a): gc_013/gc_023/bug40261/bug39438 + nine PHPT fixtures to ^:slow; the quick selection asserts a recorded mismatch manifest (105 IDs, family counts: GC 10, foreach-by-ref 16, unset CV 4, named params 3, other 72; php-src 8.3.35 tag-pinned).\n17\t4. gc_013 three-way: the docker php:8.3 oracle gives bool(true)/ok (the pin is right); the ENGINE lacks gc_collect_cycles entirely (undefined function) -> the known-gap row wording is in the manifest/findings.\n18\t5. The foreach_016 engine defect fixed (3321ecee: by-ref foreach cursor preserved across array_unshift reindexing).\n19\t6. The FOO constant refusal fixed (bf8c9c20) with a known over-refusal on the ns-use-function-const path under a separate reconciliation round (a corpus DIFF probe, not an assertion failure).\n20\t7. The conformance composition (d145085b + edc50134 + a77c4b0d): real-source PHP<->TS through the convention, donors published as values, foreign cells admitted, no call-node rewriting.\n21\t8. The deps stack fix (82b78294: :test alias -Xss64m).\n22\t\n23\t## The shiva verdict\n24\t\n25\tThe FULL yang.php JVM subsystem at the tip: 16 ns / 129 tests / 4323 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors, INCLUDING e2e (the previous wedge class closed by the re-tiering). cljstyle rc=0; kondo 0/0.\n26\t\n27\t## The question\n28\t\n29\tDoes checkpoint B close? Walk your original ruling conditions one by one against this evidence (read the findings files under collab/ in the MAIN checkout /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/orch-lane/ if you need detail: the heap chain findings are 1793506..., 1793515...; the triage is 1793740...; the selection 1793860...). Rule: (a) closed — the P4 landing proceeds; (b) closed with named riders (list them, e.g. the GC known-gap row, the const-resolution round); or (c) not closed (name what is missing). Also state whether the generator fixture enablement (the S7 generators-v1 fixtures' :requires :p4-s8 activation) is now authorized."}
