{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_dGEVMYP3ylTyo6bT5BAhhL11","content":"1\t# P4 e2e red triage\n2\t\n3\t## Bare constant refusal\n4\t\n5\t`constant-node` lowered unresolved unqualified constants in the global\n6\tnamespace to `php/const-get-fq`. That moved `<?php echo FOO;` from the required\n7\tlowering refusal into runtime undefined-constant handling, so\n8\t`refusals-are-named-test` saw no `:yang.php/unsupported` diagnostic. The\n9\tlowerer now refuses that global bare-name case with `:construct :constant`;\n10\tnamespace fallback and qualified runtime lookups remain intact.\n11\t\n12\tFocused verification: `refusals-are-named-test`, 1 test / 22 assertions / 0\n13\tfailures / 0 errors.\n14\t\n15\t## PHPT quick mismatch disposition\n16\t\n17\tAdded `test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_quick_mismatch_manifest.edn`. The quick\n18\tselection test compares the exact observed failing entry IDs against the\n19\tmanifest, checks every recorded PHPT description, validates the per-feature\n20\tcounts, and asserts the unsupported count. GC and foreach rows name their\n21\tengine work items. This keeps a change from silently removing or adding a\n22\tmismatch while allowing the selection to report its known gaps honestly.\n23\t\n24\tAt this tree, the selected 271 entries report 108 pass, 58 unsupported, and\n25\t105 manifested failures. The previous 115-failure / 48-unsupported report\n26\tpredates the bare-constant diagnostic fix; ten constant cases now refuse\n27\tduring lowering. The 105 failure IDs are distributed as follows:\n28\t\n29\t| Feature | Count |\n30\t| --- | ---: |\n31\t| Zend regression cases | 70 |\n32\t| GC cycle collection | 10 |\n33\t| Foreach mutation/reference semantics | 11 |\n34\t| Named parameter binding | 3 |\n35\t| Unset CV behavior | 4 |\n36\t| Array references | 1 |\n37\t| Pass by reference | 5 |\n38\t| Array internal pointer | 1 |\n39\t\n40\t## Thrown error\n41\t\n42\tThe requested quick namespace rerun completed without a thrown test error:\n43\t20 tests / 1,116 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors. The earlier single error\n44\twas not reproduced at this tip; this clean run does not identify its original\n45\tstack. The PHPT worker catches engine throws and classifies them as entry\n46\tfailures, so the prior error was outside that per-entry catch.\n47\t\n48\t## `gc_013` oracle cross-check\n49\t\n50\tThe pinned row is `Zend/tests/gc_013.phpt`; source builds 10,001 self-reference\n51\tcycles, then prints the result of `gc_collect_cycles() > 0` followed by `ok`.\n52\tThe pinned expectation is `bool(true)\\nok`. `phpt/matches-expect?` trims\n53\ttrailing whitespace and compares the actual body, so the recorded source and\n54\tcomparison shape are consistent on inspection.\n55\t\n56\tOn shiva, ran the exact pinned source through `docker run --rm -i\n57\tphp:8.3.35-cli` under `timeout 300`. The real oracle printed:\n58\t\n59\t```text\n60\tbool(true)\n61\tok\n62\t```\n63\t\n64\tThis matches the recorded pin exactly. The local engine stress test completed\n65\tin about six minutes with\n66\t`{:out \"\", :diag [], :uncaught {:class \"Error\", :message \"Call to undefined function gc_collect_cycles()\"}}`.\n67\tThe three-way result is therefore:\n68\t\n69\t| Source | Result |\n70\t| --- | --- |\n71\t| Pinned `phpt_selection.edn` | `bool(true)\\nok` |\n72\t| Docker PHP 8.3.35 on shiva | `bool(true)` then `ok`; matches pin |\n73\t| Engine | Empty output, then uncaught `Error: Call to undefined function gc_collect_cycles()` |\n74\t\n75\tAdded this as `:slow-known-gaps` in the mismatch manifest, with the oracle pin,\n76\tengine result, and named GC work item. The slow PHPT stress test checks this\n77\trecorded result explicitly. Proposed gap wording: **“PHP cyclic garbage\n78\tcollection is not implemented; `gc_013` self-referential cycles are not\n79\tcollected, so `gc_collect_cycles()` does not return a positive cycle count.”**\n80\t\n81\t## Verification\n82\t\n83\t- PHP e2e quick namespace: 20 tests / 1,116 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors.\n84\t- PHPT quick manifest test after adding the slow `gc_013` known-gap row: 1\n85\t  test / 5 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors (271 entries: 108 pass, 58\n86\t  unsupported, 105 manifested failures).\n87\t- `gc_013` engine stress test: one expected known-gap mismatch with the exact\n88\t  recorded engine result above; its slow test now asserts that result and the\n89\t  pinned oracle text.\n90\t- `cljstyle check` on the changed Clojure files: clean.\n91\t- clj-kondo on the changed Clojure files: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n92\t- `git diff --check`: clean.\n93\t- PHP literal/runtime, class model, include, lower-portable, and scope consumers:\n94\t  46 tests / 1,975 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors.\n95\t- The full `bb test:sub:clj yang.php` attempt was stopped after 13 minutes\n96\t  without a summary in e2e; the standalone e2e gate and focused consumers above\n97\t  completed successfully.\n98\t\n99\t## Commits\n100\t\n101\t- `6dee9f26 test(yang.php): record PHPT quick mismatch manifest`\n102\t- `bf8c9c20 fix(yang.php): refuse unresolved global constants`\n103\t\n104\tBoth commits are on `yang-php-p4`; neither was pushed. This findings file is\n105\tuncommitted as requested."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_fC3nyh6bAlCHPmtRPstxnZqb","content":"1\t# PHP reachable-heap fixture correction findings\n2\t\n3\t## Fixture correction\n4\t\n5\t`live-after-collection` now mirrors the Python measurement protocol. It runs\n6\tthe PHP unit through normal completion with no injected blocker, locates the\n7\tsuspended generator `h` in the final heap, asserts that exactly one matching\n8\tcell exists, and calls `engine/collect` with that cell reference as an extra\n9\troot. The source keeps `$it->self = $it`, preserving the suspended generator\n10\tthrough its deliberate cycle after module cleanup.\n11\t\n12\tThe N=10/N=1000 equality assertion is unchanged. The generator runtime and\n13\tcleanup code were not modified.\n14\t\n15\t## Result\n16\t\n17\tThe corrected fixture still grows on every VM. These are final-heap results\n18\tafter normal completion and collection rooted at the suspended `h`:\n19\t\n20\t| VM | N=10 cells / deep size | N=1000 cells / deep size |\n21\t|---|---:|---:|\n22\t| AST walker | 151 / 171,275 | 5,596 / 992,480 |\n23\t| Semantic | 151 / 23,253 | 5,596 / 792,483 |\n24\t| Stack | 151 / 131,268 | 5,596 / 708,933 |\n25\t| Register | 151 / 444,280 | 5,596 / 1,160,545 |\n26\t\n27\tThis corrected result warrants a runtime retention investigation. It does not\n28\tjustify changing the fixture or weakening its equality assertion.\n29\t\n30\t## Verification\n31\t\n32\t- Explicit slow test: `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n yang.php.antlr.generators-test`\n33\t  — **1 test, 12 assertions, 4 failures, 0 errors**. The four failures are the\n34\t  expected N=10/N=1000 equality mismatches above; all four one-suspended-`h`\n35\t  root assertions passed.\n36\t- `cljstyle check test/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj`: passed.\n37\t- `clojure -M:kondo --lint test/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj`:\n38\t  **0 errors, 0 warnings**.\n39\t- `git diff --check`: clean."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_nsOvyR3V4ox8VLC3dazPyE8W","content":"1\t# PHP P4 S8 generator resume-chain retention findings\n2\t\n3\tBranch: `yang-php-p4`; starting commit: `18ef324d`.\n4\t\n5\t## Requested change\n6\t\n7\t`php/gen-enter` now rebuilds the running state from an empty map. It keeps\n8\t`:name`, `:cleanup`, `:current`, `:key`, and `:next-key`, installs the active\n9\t`:return` and `:caller-ctx`, and omits `:resume`, `:ctx`, and `:body`.\n10\tNo destructor releases were added; the corrected reachable-heap fixture and\n11\tits equality assertion are unchanged.\n12\t\n13\tThe old suspended state remains the local `s` used by the same invocation to\n14\trestore `php.rt/ctx` and invoke `:resume`. Those are the only readers of the\n15\tsuspension fields in the PHP runtime. Cleanup remains necessary for created\n16\tand suspended generator destruction, so it is preserved.\n17\t\n18\t## Exact-scope gate result\n19\t\n20\tThe prescribed `gen-enter` rebuild alone does **not** close the regression.\n21\tThe explicit slow test still fails equality on all four VMs; all eight\n22\tsingle-suspended-`h` root checks pass. Measured values are `[live cells,\n23\tdeep-size structural units]`, not bytes:\n24\t\n25\t| VM | N=10 | N=1000 |\n26\t|---|---:|---:|\n27\t| AST walker | 151 / 171,339 | 5,596 / 984,624 |\n28\t| Semantic | 151 / 23,191 | 5,596 / 784,501 |\n29\t| Stack | 151 / 131,282 | 5,596 / 701,027 |\n30\t| Register | 151 / 444,408 | 5,596 / 1,152,753 |\n31\t\n32\tThe focused runner executes `clojure.test/run-tests` on the entire generators,\n33\tobjects, and class-model namespaces, with no quick-tier exclusion. Its only\n34\tinstrumentation wraps the existing private measurement function to print its\n35\treturn value; collection roots, PHP source, and assertions are untouched.\n36\t\n37\tCommand:\n38\t\n39\t```sh\n40\tclojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:p4-gate {:extra-paths [\"test\"]}}}' \\\n41\t  -M:p4-gate /private/tmp/p4-resume-chain-gate.clj\n42\t```\n43\t\n44\tLog: `target/profile/p4-resume-chain-focused.log`.\n45\t\n46\t## Remaining investigation\n47\t\n48\t`php/yield-raw` still copies the running state into the suspended state,\n49\tincluding the caller's `:return` and `:caller-ctx`. Also, `php/yield` keeps its\n50\tlocal running state `s` alive across the call to `php/yield-raw`. The Python\n51\tprelude rebuilds both running and suspended states and its yield wrapper\n52\tdoes not hold such a state snapshot across suspension.\n53\t\n54\tA repository-independent, in-memory experiment is prepared at\n55\t`/private/tmp/p4-resume-chain-diagnose.clj` to test these additional paths.\n56\tThe user was asked whether the explicitly bounded source scope may be widened\n57\tif this experiment proves additional changes necessary.\n58\t\n59\t## Validation so far\n60\t\n61\t- `cljstyle check src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc`: passed.\n62\t- `clojure -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc`: 0 errors,\n63\t  0 warnings.\n64\t- `git diff --check`: passed.\n65\t\n66\t## Additional retention evidence (in-memory only)\n67\t\n68\tThe exact-scope focused run finished: **14 tests, 1,201 assertions, 4\n69\tfailures, 0 errors**. The only failures were the four retention equalities.\n70\t\n71\tOn the semantic VM, comparing N=10 / N=20:\n72\t\n73\t| Experiment on top of the requested rebuild | N=10 | N=20 |\n74\t|---|---:|---:|\n75\t| Also rebuild suspended state | 151 / 23,151 | 206 / 30,801 |\n76\t| Also remove `php/yield`'s local state snapshot | 151 / 22,851 | 206 / 30,201 |\n77\t| Also return null from `php/gen-put!` | 99 / 16,043 | 99 / 16,043 |\n78\t\n79\tThe trace of the second experiment gives the concrete retained edge:\n80\t\n81\t```text\n82\th.gen.resume.payload.k[15].env.%_\n83\t  -> running-state.return.payload.env.s\n84\t  -> previous-suspended-state.resume.payload.k[15].env.%_\n85\t  -> ...\n86\t```\n87\t\n88\tThe lowered `do` binds the previous expression's result as `%_`.\n89\t`php/gen-put!` returns the whole state; the discarded result of the\n90\t`php/yield` state update therefore holds the running snapshot (including\n91\t`:return`) across capture even after the explicit local `s` is removed.\n92\tEvery `php/gen-put!` caller ignores its return value. Returning `:php/null`\n93\tpreserves its side effect and avoids retaining that snapshot.\n94\t\n95\tA candidate consisting of the requested rebuild plus three narrow changes\n96\tis under explicit N=10/N=1000 verification **in memory only**:\n97\t\n98\t1. Rebuild the suspended state in `php/yield-raw`, preserving metadata and\n99\t   iteration state but omitting `:return` and `:caller-ctx`.\n100\t2. Remove `php/yield`'s local running-state snapshot across capture.\n101\t3. Make `php/gen-put!` return `:php/null` rather than the updated state.\n102\t\n103\tNo destructor changes are involved. The working-tree source remains limited\n104\tto the originally requested `gen-enter` change pending scope clarification.\n105\t\n106\t## Expanded candidate: unchanged slow regression passes\n107\t\n108\tThe in-memory expanded candidate passes the original slow test: **1 test,\n109\t12 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**. This includes both root checks and\n110\texact equality of the complete measurement on every VM:\n111\t\n112\t| VM | N=10 | N=1000 |\n113\t|---|---:|---:|\n114\t| AST walker | 99 / 163,823 | 99 / 163,823 |\n115\t| Semantic | 99 / 16,043 | 99 / 16,043 |\n116\t| Stack | 99 / 125,976 | 99 / 125,976 |\n117\t| Register | 99 / 437,914 | 99 / 437,914 |\n118\t\n119\tCommand:\n120\t\n121\t```sh\n122\tclojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:p4-gate {:extra-paths [\"test\"]}}}' \\\n123\t  -M:p4-gate /private/tmp/p4-resume-chain-candidate-gate.clj\n124\t```\n125\t\n126\tLog: `target/profile/p4-resume-chain-candidate-gate.log`.\n127\t\n128\tThe source proposal is at\n129\t`/private/tmp/p4-resume-chain-proposal/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc`; its diff\n130\tagainst the scoped worktree patch is\n131\t`/private/tmp/p4-resume-chain-proposal.patch`. The proposal passes cljstyle\n132\tusing the repository's `.cljstyle` configuration.\n133\t\n134\tThe broader quick tier is running against the **actual scoped worktree**\n135\tusing `bb test:sub:clj yang.php` (log:\n136\t`target/profile/p4-resume-chain-php-quick.log`).\n137\t\n138\t## Handoff status\n139\t\n140\tScope clarification is still pending. The actual worktree contains only the\n141\trequested `gen-enter` rebuild. It is **not committed**, because its mandatory\n142\tretention regression remains red; nothing has been pushed. The expanded\n143\tcandidate has not been applied to the worktree.\n144\t\n145\tThe expanded source proposal also passes kondo: **0 errors, 0 warnings**.\n146\tThe broader scoped PHP quick run is still active in the e2e namespace at this\n147\thandoff; no complete quick-tier result is claimed. Its exec session is 19232,\n148\tand `target/profile/sub-clj.log` contains the test output. The wrapper log is\n149\t`target/profile/p4-resume-chain-php-quick.log`.\n150\t\n151\t## Authorized extension: final implementation\n152\t\n153\tThe user explicitly authorized the extension after the initial scoped result.\n154\tThis section and the final validation below supersede the earlier pending-scope\n155\thandoff. The implementation is now applied to the actual worktree, not an\n156\tin-memory override.\n157\t\n158\tChanged source file: `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc`.\n159\tAll four changed touchpoints:\n160\t\n161\t1. `php/gen-put!` (line 4278): still updates the generator object cell, but\n162\t   returns `:php/null` rather than the state map. No caller consumes its\n163\t   return value. This prevents lowered `do`'s discarded `%_` binding from\n164\t   retaining a running-state snapshot across continuation capture.\n165\t2. `php/gen-enter` (line 4306): rebuilds running state from an empty map,\n166\t   preserving `:name`, `:cleanup`, `:current`, `:key`, and `:next-key`, and\n167\t   installing the current `:return` and `:caller-ctx`. It drops old `:resume`,\n168\t   `:ctx`, and initial `:body` fields.\n169\t3. `php/yield-raw` (line 4338): rebuilds suspended state from an empty map,\n170\t   preserving the same metadata/iteration fields and installing only the\n171\t   current `:resume` and `:ctx`. It drops `:return` and `:caller-ctx`.\n172\t4. `php/yield` (line 4360): passes `(php/gen-state g)` directly to\n173\t   `php/gen-next-key!` instead of binding the running state to local `s`\n174\t   across `php/yield-raw`'s capture. Only the resulting key stays live.\n175\t\n176\tRestore-path audit: `gen-enter` still restores the prior suspension's `:ctx`\n177\tand invokes its `:resume` from its local incoming `s`, after publishing the\n178\tfresh running state. `yield-raw` still restores `:caller-ctx` and invokes\n179\t`:return` from its local incoming running state after publishing the fresh\n180\tsuspended state. No other runtime reader depends on those discarded fields\n181\tremaining in the object. Created/suspended destruction still gets the preserved\n182\t`:cleanup`, and current values, keys, and automatic next-key state remain\n183\tavailable. No destructor/release behavior was changed.\n184\t\n185\tThe existing corrected `test/yang/php/antlr/generators_test.clj` is unchanged,\n186\tincluding PHP source, roots, deep-size traversal, and exact equality assertion.\n187\t\n188\t### Final focused JVM validation\n189\t\n190\tOn the actual final worktree, `/private/tmp/p4-resume-chain-gate.clj` executed\n191\tall three consumer namespaces with no slow exclusion: **14 tests, 1,201\n192\tassertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**, exit 0. The slow heap test ran explicitly\n193\twithin that invocation; its eight measurements were logged unchanged.\n194\t\n195\t+------------+---------------------------+---------------------------+\n196\t| VM         | N=10 cells / deep size    | N=1000 cells / deep size  |\n197\t+============+===========================+===========================+\n198\t| AST walker | 99 / 163,823              | 99 / 163,823              |\n199\t+------------+---------------------------+---------------------------+\n200\t| Semantic   | 99 / 16,043               | 99 / 16,043               |\n201\t+------------+---------------------------+---------------------------+\n202\t| Stack      | 99 / 125,976              | 99 / 125,976              |\n203\t+------------+---------------------------+---------------------------+\n204\t| Register   | 99 / 437,914              | 99 / 437,914              |\n205\t+------------+---------------------------+---------------------------+\n206\t\n207\tThese are structural deep-size counts, not bytes. All one-suspended-`h`\n208\troot checks and exact N=10/N=1000 equalities pass. Final focused log:\n209\t`target/profile/p4-resume-chain-final-focused.log`.\n210\t\n211\t### PHP subsystem quick tier\n212\t\n213\t`bb test:sub yang.php` selects 16 JVM namespaces and four each on Node/Dart.\n214\tThe first Dart attempt failed before tests because the sandbox denied writes\n215\tto Flutter's installed cache (`engine.stamp.tmp` and `engine.realm`), followed\n216\tby the compiler's EOF error when Flutter supplied no analyzer response.\n217\tEvidence: `target/profile/p4-resume-chain-dart-sandbox.log`.\n218\tThe JVM and Node lanes continue; Dart will be rerun with the cache access\n219\tneeded for this explicitly requested validation after the other lanes finish.\n220\t\n221\tNode quick lane completed successfully: **50 tests, 2,226 assertions,\n222\t0 failures, 0 errors**, exit 0; compiler summary: 137 files, 136 compiled,\n223\t0 warnings. Log: `target/profile/sub-cljs.log`.\n224\t\n225\tFinal source lint checks completed successfully:\n226\t\n227\t- `cljstyle check src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc`: passed.\n228\t- `clojure -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc`: **0 errors,\n229\t  0 warnings**.\n230\t- `git diff --check`: passed.\n231\t\n232\tThe source blob validated by the focused test and these lint checks is\n233\t`3f767747b7656ed6d566e3ce006b57f8447d52a5`. Only the one source file is intended\n234\tfor the commit; this findings file and pre-existing collab artifacts remain\n235\tuncommitted.\n236\t\n237\tDart retry completed successfully with the needed Flutter cache permissions:\n238\t`bb test:sub:cljd yang.php` — **4 namespaces, 50 tests, 0 failures**, exit 0,\n239\t165 seconds. Flutter reports `All tests passed!`; it does not report an\n240\tassertion total. Logs: `target/profile/p4-resume-chain-final-dart-quick.log`\n241\tand `target/profile/sub-cljd.log`. No other Dart compilation was active.\n242\tThe retry ran within the same PHP validation set while the long JVM PHPT\n243\tselection continued, matching the original runner's parallel lane schedule.\n244\t\n245\tThe JVM quick selection includes 280 active PHPT entries out of 1,088 recorded\n246\tentries; the other 808 have `:needs` and are deferred by the existing test.\n247\tIt includes `Zend/tests/bug40261.phpt` with three 100,000-iteration loops,\n248\tplus other allocator/GC stress fixtures. A non-terminating JVM thread dump\n249\tconfirmed the process was actively executing `phpt-selection-runs-test`\n250\t(`e2e_test.clj:340`) through `engine-result` and the AST walker. No test tags,\n251\tcase selection, fixture source, or iteration limits were changed to shorten\n252\tthis gate. The thread dump is embedded in `target/profile/sub-clj.log`.\n253\t\n254\t### Broad JVM quick timeout\n255\t\n256\tThe original unmodified JVM quick attempt was stopped after **3,575 seconds\n257\t(59 min 35 sec)** in `phpt-selection-runs-test`, with no aggregate test result.\n258\tThe process was still using 99.4% CPU (60 min 38 sec accumulated CPU time),\n259\tRSS 661,248 KiB. It received SIGTERM; the child exited 143 and the initial\n260\ttri-host wrapper exited 1. The complete log is preserved at\n261\t`target/profile/sub-clj.log`; wrapper summary:\n262\t`target/profile/p4-resume-chain-final-php-quick.log`.\n263\t\n264\t**No complete broader JVM quick gate is claimed.** No fixture iterations or\n265\ttest metadata were changed. This is a validation timeout, not an assertion\n266\tfailure attributed to the generator fix. No baseline-comparison run was made,\n267\tso this report does not assert that the stress runtime is a proved baseline\n268\tregression or a newly introduced regression.\n269\t\n270\tTo cover the remaining JVM quick tests after the stalled phase, a temporary\n271\trunner is executing all 16 selected namespaces with the standard `:slow`\n272\texclusion and only the already-timed-out `phpt-selection-runs-test` omitted\n273\tfrom this repeat. The timeout remains part of the overall validation result;\n274\ta successful remainder run cannot make the complete broad gate green.\n275\tNo repository test file is changed. Runner:\n276\t`/private/tmp/p4-resume-chain-quick-remainder.clj`; log:\n277\t`target/profile/p4-resume-chain-final-php-quick-remainder.log`.\n278\t\n279\tRemainder-runner correction: the first temporary remainder runner attempted\n280\tfiltering by redefining `clojure.test/test-vars`. The compiled Clojure test\n281\tlibrary calls that function statically, bypassing the Var replacement. A\n282\tthread dump caught it running the slow `fixtures-on-every-vm-test`; that run\n283\twas stopped and is not used as quick-tier evidence. Its log is preserved at\n284\t`target/profile/p4-resume-chain-php-remainder-invalid-filter.log`.\n285\t\n286\tThe corrected temporary runner uses the official Cognitect runner's strategy:\n287\tit removes `:test` metadata in this process from `:slow` vars and the one\n288\talready-timed-out PHPT selection var. It asserts those exclusions before\n289\texecution and logs the complete excluded-var list, selected count, and every\n290\ttest var as it starts. No repository test source or fixture is changed.\n291\tThe completed focused gate used no exclusion and is unaffected by this\n292\trunner issue; its eight measurements and 14-test summary remain valid.\n293\t\n294\t### Completed JVM quick remainder\n295\t\n296\tThe corrected runner finished all 16 selected namespaces with **124 tests,\n297\t4,316 assertions, 2 failures, 0 errors**, exit 1. The selected count was\n298\tverified before execution; the excluded list consists of the seven normal\n299\t`:slow` tests and the one PHPT selection test already attempted for 3,575 s.\n300\tThe original heap regression was separately run in full and passed.\n301\t\n302\tBoth remaining assertion failures are in\n303\t`yang.php.antlr.e2e-test/refusals-are-named-test` (`e2e_test.clj:103-104`),\n304\tfor source `<?php echo FOO;`. The assertions expect compile-time diagnostic\n305\t`:yang.php/unsupported` with construct `:constant`, but get no such diagnostic.\n306\tNo other assertion failures or errors occurred in the remainder run.\n307\tLog: `target/profile/p4-resume-chain-final-php-quick-remainder.log`.\n308\t\n309\tA focused comparison against the original `18ef324d` prelude is running for\n310\tthat exact test var. The baseline source blob is\n311\t`835ea7eb4271a35187c0fb9105cb7173209d76f8`, matching both `git show 18ef324d:...`\n312\tand the temporary baseline source file's hash. The baseline runner prints the\n313\tactual classpath resource and asserts the old setter definition is loaded.\n314\tAll other tracked sources are unchanged, so this isolates the generator patch.\n315\t\n316\t### Baseline comparison completed\n317\t\n318\tThe original `18ef324d` prelude reproduces the **identical two `FOO` failures**:\n319\t**1 test, 22 assertions, 2 failures, 0 errors**, exit 1. Both failing assertions\n320\thave the same expected/actual values and line numbers as the final-code\n321\tremainder run. Thus these two assertion failures predate this generator fix.\n322\tNo unrelated refusal-test expectation was changed.\n323\t\n324\tCommand:\n325\t\n326\t```sh\n327\tclojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:p4-baseline {:extra-paths [\"/private/tmp/p4-resume-chain-baseline\" \"test\"]}}}' \\\n328\t  -M:p4-baseline /private/tmp/p4-resume-chain-baseline-check.clj\n329\t```\n330\t\n331\tLog: `target/profile/p4-resume-chain-baseline-failures.log`.\n332\tThe full broader JVM quick gate is **not green**: its PHPT selection was\n333\tcapped at 3,575 seconds, and the completed 124-test remainder contains these\n334\ttwo baseline assertion failures. The focused generator/object/class-model\n335\tvalidation, including the unchanged heap regression, passes completely.\n336\t\n337\t## Final committed result\n338\t\n339\tCommitted on `yang-php-p4`:\n340\t`4c8eaacf91bae7202249c88c280877e5ae5216f9`\n341\t(`fix(yang.php): stop retaining generator resume history`). **Not pushed.**\n342\t\n343\tThe commit contains only `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc` (15 insertions,\n344\t5 deletions), with these four touchpoints:\n345\t\n346\t1. `php/gen-put!` (4278): returns `:php/null` to prevent a discarded state-map\n347\t   result surviving as lowered `do`'s `%_` across capture.\n348\t2. `php/gen-enter` (4306): rebuilds running state, preserving metadata and\n349\t   iteration state but dropping old `:resume`, `:ctx`, and initial `:body`.\n350\t3. `php/yield-raw` (4338): rebuilds suspended state and drops caller-only\n351\t   `:return` and `:caller-ctx` fields.\n352\t4. `php/yield` (4360): removes the running-state local across the yield capture.\n353\t\n354\tNo destructor releases or repository test/fixture changes were added. The\n355\trestore paths continue using their local incoming states, as audited above.\n356\t\n357\tFinal measured reachable heaps, after normal PHP completion and collection:\n358\t\n359\t+------------+---------------------------+---------------------------+\n360\t| VM         | N=10 cells / deep size    | N=1000 cells / deep size  |\n361\t+============+===========================+===========================+\n362\t| AST walker | 99 / 163,823              | 99 / 163,823              |\n363\t+------------+---------------------------+---------------------------+\n364\t| Semantic   | 99 / 16,043               | 99 / 16,043               |\n365\t+------------+---------------------------+---------------------------+\n366\t| Stack      | 99 / 125,976              | 99 / 125,976              |\n367\t+------------+---------------------------+---------------------------+\n368\t| Register   | 99 / 437,914              | 99 / 437,914              |\n369\t+------------+---------------------------+---------------------------+\n370\t\n371\tFinal validation:\n372\t\n373\t- **Required heap gate and full generators/objects/class-model namespaces:**\n374\t  14 tests, 1,201 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors. The unchanged slow heap test\n375\t  ran with all eight measurements; every root check and equality passed.\n376\t- **Broader JVM quick tier:** not green. The unmodified PHPT-selection test\n377\t  attempt was capped at 3,575 seconds. The completed remainder ran 124 tests\n378\t  and 4,316 assertions with 2 failures, 0 errors. The exact two failures were\n379\t  reproduced using the original `18ef324d` prelude (1 test, 22 assertions,\n380\t  2 failures, 0 errors), proving those assertion failures predate this fix.\n381\t- **Node quick tier:** 4 namespaces, 50 tests, 2,226 assertions, 0 failures,\n382\t  0 errors; compiler 0 warnings.\n383\t- **Dart quick tier:** 4 namespaces, 50 tests, 0 failures, exit 0, after retry\n384\t  with Flutter cache access. Flutter reports all tests passed.\n385\t- **Lint:** cljstyle passed; kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings; whitespace checks\n386\t  passed.\n387\t\n388\tPost-commit verification confirms the formatter hook left the tested source\n389\tblob unchanged: `3f767747b7656ed6d566e3ce006b57f8447d52a5`. The commit's file\n390\tlist and diff match the reviewed one-file patch. There are no tracked working\n391\tchanges. This findings file and the three pre-existing flat collab artifacts\n392\tremain uncommitted. No complete broader JVM quick pass is claimed."}
