{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_bmT4TU9uSy2BFGD12ONsKoip","content":"1\t# Checkpoint-B fold reconciliation findings\n2\t\n3\t## What failed\n4\t\n5\tThe focused JVM run initially failed one assertion in\n6\t`p4-registry-is-inert-test`. It expected every value in `p4/generators-v1` to\n7\tcarry `p4/banner`, but that var is the raw generator fixture definitions. The\n8\tfolded values, including recorded oracle values and hand-pinned outputs, are in\n9\t`p4/all-fixtures`; unrecorded raw definitions remain `:pending`.\n10\t\n11\t## True post-fold invariants\n12\t\n13\t- `p4/awaiting-oracle` equals exactly the IDs of enabled fixtures whose folded\n14\t  `:oracle` is `:pending`.\n15\t- For each ID in `p4/recorded`, the matching folded fixture's `:out`, `:diag`,\n16\t  and `:uncaught` equal the recorded values. A recorded fixture has the oracle\n17\t  banner because it has a recorded result.\n18\t- Generator metadata such as `:requires` is checked on the raw\n19\t  `p4/generators-v1` definitions. Oracle state is checked on the generator\n20\t  members of `p4/all-fixtures`: the banner is expected when a record exists or\n21\t  an output is pinned; otherwise the fixture remains `:pending`.\n22\t\n23\t## Change made\n24\t\n25\tUpdated the inert-registry description and replaced the incorrect assertion on\n26\traw generator definitions with a per-fixture check against the folded\n27\t`p4/all-fixtures` view. The enabled-pending equality and recorded field\n28\tcross-check remain exact. No fixture pins or protected source files were\n29\tchanged.\n30\t\n31\t## Verification\n32\t\n33\t- Class-model namespace: **8 tests, 587 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n34\t- All `programs-p4` consumer namespaces (`class-model-test`, `generators-test`,\n35\t  `objects-test`): **14 tests, 1,076 assertions, 6 failures, 1 error**.\n36\t  - Four failures are the reachable-heap stability assertion, one per VM. Each\n37\t    measured 151 reachable cells at 10 iterations and 5,596 at 1,000\n38\t    iterations, consistent with the branch's checkpoint-B heap measurement.\n39\t  - `objects-test` has two output mismatches (`decl-byref-param-typed-coerces`\n40\t    and `decl-byref-later-rejection-releases-earlier-param`) and one runtime\n41\t    error (`data primitive refused`, `str-concat`, wrong type). Those tests and\n42\t    the heap measurement are outside this task's authorized change scope.\n43\t- `cljstyle check test/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc`: passed.\n44\t- `clojure -M:kondo --lint test/yang/php/antlr/class_model_test.cljc test/yang/php/antlr/programs_p4.cljc`:\n45\t  **0 errors, 0 warnings**."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_M8NNAOfUaxf8fxk5j9c0Jp6l","content":"1\t# PHPT selection failure payload and applicability\n2\t\n3\t## Change\n4\t\n5\t`phpt-selection-runs-test` now summarizes known gaps as five counts (`gc`,\n6\t`foreach-by-ref`, `unset-cv`, `named-params`, `other`) and the mismatch ID\n7\tlist. It no longer compares feature-count maps or reports engine-result maps\n8\ton assertion failure. The no-manifest fallback also reports only IDs. The\n9\tquick mismatch manifest records php-src tag `8.3.35`, and the test checks it\n10\tagainst the committed selection tag.\n11\t\n12\t## Environment evidence\n13\t\n14\t- The committed selection is tagged `8.3.35`, with 1,088 total rows and 271\n15\t  quick rows after `:needs`/`:slow` filtering.\n16\t- `test/resources/php-src` is absent in this checkout. The test does not read\n17\t  that path: it consumes the checked-in `phpt_selection.edn`.\n18\t- Selection generation accepts a caller-supplied php-src root\n19\t  (`src/dev/yang/php/phpt.clj`). Thus an unpinned or different generated\n20\t  selection could change the test inputs; the added tag assertion makes such\n21\t  drift fail explicitly.\n22\t- The PHPT runner calls `e2e-harness/run-raw`, which runs the AST walker. The\n23\t  four-VM set (`:ast-walker`, `:semantic`, `:stack`, `:register`) is used by\n24\t  the separate fixture test, not by this PHPT comparison.\n25\t- This checkout has no connection or mounted path for the shiva clone, so its\n26\t  `test/resources/php-src` presence and VM configuration cannot be inspected\n27\t  from here. The provided shiva report identifies the output-printing failure,\n28\t  but does not include the differing ID set. Local selection data alone\n29\t  cannot establish whether that remote run used different selected rows or\n30\t  exposed only the unbounded assertion printer.\n31\t\n32\t## Verification\n33\t\n34\t`bb test:sub:clj yang.php` reached the local PHPT result at default JVM stack:\n35\t271 quick rows, 108 pass, 58 unsupported, and 105 manifested mismatches. The\n36\tobserved mismatch IDs matched the manifest; no engine-result payload appeared.\n37\tThe manifest-derived family counts are `gc=10`, `foreach-by-ref=16`,\n38\t`unset-cv=4`, `named-params=3`, `other=72`; they agree with both the pinned\n39\tfamily source counts and the manifest ID families.\n40\t\n41\tThe aggregate subsystem run was interrupted while an existing `zz-probe2-test`\n42\twas printing per-fixture diagnostics; it did not produce an aggregate summary.\n43\tThe PHPT test had already completed, and no failure/error was reported before\n44\tthe probe. Focused PHP consumers completed separately: 46 tests / 1,975\n45\tassertions / 0 failures / 0 errors (`yang.php-test`, literal, class model,\n46\tinclude, lower-portable, and scope namespaces).\n47\t\n48\t`cljstyle check`, clj-kondo (0 errors, 0 warnings), and `git diff --check` are\n49\tclean. The shiva clone itself is not mounted in this workspace, so its corpus\n50\tdirectory and runtime VM configuration remain unverified here."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_TS2qh6RQb88mi0bpHRFRb81X","content":"1\t# PHP admission of foreign `yang.call` cells\n2\t\n3\t## Implementation\n4\t\n5\t- PHP's bundled prelude now includes the shared `yang.call` definitions.\n6\t- `php/resolve-fn` admits only function-table values that pass\n7\t  `yang.call/eligible?`; non-conforming values retain the undefined-function\n8\t  error.\n9\t- PHP callable checks and resolution recognize an existing shared entry\n10\t  structurally. `php/call`, named calls, and binding-profile calls now route\n11\t  through `yang.call/invoke` / `invoke-with`.\n12\t- PHP's linked program requires `yang.call` before `php`, and the PHP module\n13\t  pins its `yang.call` content address. The linked harness publishes and names\n14\t  both modules.\n15\t- Strict identity compares a shared callable with itself before PHP's local\n16\t  type interpretation. This lets a TS function cell survive PHP global and\n17\t  array storage and pass `===` without interpreting its foreign value layout.\n18\t- Added a real lowered TS-to-PHP test: the TS cell is placed in a PHP global,\n19\t  stored in a PHP array, called from PHP source, and checked for strict\n20\t  identity. The TS callback returns `undefined`; its result is deliberately\n21\t  discarded because cross-language value interpretation is outside this\n22\t  admission change.\n23\t\n24\t## Verification\n25\t\n26\t- New callback test, direct TS-export PHP call, bundled-prelude closure check,\n27\t  and PHP module-spec test: pass on JVM.\n28\t- Linked-profile equivalence test: pass on semantic, stack, and register VMs.\n29\t- PHP class-model, objects, and generators namespaces: 14 tests / 1,201\n30\t  assertions pass.\n31\t- `cljstyle check`, clj-kondo, and `git diff --check`: clean.\n32\t- The broad fast PHP e2e + prelude run is not green on this checkout. It reports\n33\t  the existing PHPT quick-selection mismatches (271 entries: 108 pass, 48\n34\t  unsupported, 115 fail) and the existing `echo FOO` refusal expectation.\n35\t  Its first pass also found that PHP's declared host names omitted `data/nth`,\n36\t  which the newly bundled shared helper uses; that manifest omission is fixed,\n37\t  and the closed-prelude test passes on rerun. The added callback checks pass.\n38\t  A prior checkout finding\n39\t  (`collab/1793660000000-engineer-p4-yangcall-conformance.gpt-6-luna.findings.md`)\n40\t  recorded the same quick-selection and `echo FOO` failures before this change.\n41\t\n42\t## `gc_013` triage\n43\t\n44\tThe pinned PHPT entry carries the canonical source and `EXPECT` body\n45\t`bool(true)\\nok`. `phpt/matches-expect?` compares the observed output to that\n46\tbody after trimming trailing whitespace, and the stress runner reports\n47\t`:fail` only when execution throws or the output mismatches. The harness\n48\tcomparison therefore appears consistent with the pin. The likely issue is\n49\tengine behavior: this checkout also reports the nearby `gc_023` stress case\n50\tas a mismatch, and the PHP GC cycle collector is not implemented by the PHP\n51\truntime here.\n52\t\n53\tI did not run `gc_013` to completion against a PHP CLI oracle in this worktree:\n54\tno `php` executable is installed, and prior work measured its 10,001-loop\n55\twalker path at roughly 259 seconds before it reached the unsupported GC call.\n56\tTreat the expected output as authoritative; verify against the pinned PHP\n57\tCLI on shiva before changing the expectation or harness."}
